Just some general advice:

There are 5 major resistances that you must try to get as quickly as
possible: Magic resistance, reflection, magic cancellation, poison
resistance, and sleep resistance.

Of those, magic cancellation is very easy to get, and poison and sleep
resistance are generally not _too_ hard to get if you handle your meals
properly (eat elves for the latter, and quivering blobs, shriekers,
cave spiders, unicorns, etc for the former).

MR and reflection are the toughest.

You generally do not want to descend below DL8 without MR, because
things like polymorph traps and level teleport traps become very
painful to deal with.  If you must go below DL8 without it, then you
either spend a lot of time searching before each square you move (or
pet-stepping) or are at reasonably high risk of bad things happening.

There are 2 early sources of reflection, neither guaranteed: Sokoban
and Medusa.  The combination gives you a 75% chance of getting
reflection before the Castle (more, once you factor in random items
generated, A drops, bones, etc).

Your quest artifact may grant MR, although that is not a good source to
rely on in the long term (but it's much better than nothing in the
short term).

To me, that makes MR the clear choice for a first wish unless you have
it already (in which case reflection is a good choice if you lack it).

If you choose to go with gray dragon scale mail (MR) or silver dragon
scale mail (reflection) you also get good AC in a spellcasting-friendly
form.  The other reasonable alternative is an artifact that helps
survivability a lot (e.g. the Eye of the Aethiopica for spellcasters).
But generally until you're pretty comfortable using a lot of outs, DSM
gives you the best chance at surviving deeper into the dungeon.



